== fuller page ==
Spread 1 counted the hosts and rings. This page is about one bad day: a host
is away.

Each of the fifteen stands in one big ring and one small one; that is a
reading of his numbers, not a sentence of his [both].

Its big ring still has four. His rule for a big ring is "any 3/5 means
available", with "not more than two being reserved for one each of dev or
stage/test at any given time" [three]. So it stays up, and could lose one more.

Its small ring has two of three. Is that enough? His note does not say in so
many words. The shop's ring drawing writes 2/3 beside every small ring
[twothree]; the fact file calls that rule its own reading, marked "arguable"
[arguable]. Pin keeps both.

Who fixes it? Any ring can be looked at, but only the edge
ring steers: control "is effected only from the edge ring perspective", which
must "walk the edges and prove vs imbalances" before it plans the move [steer].
A change crosses between the two kinds of ring only through a host that holds
the same role in both, "functioning as a bastien" (his spelling) [bastion].

By default, people step down to the system's run-level to change a ring's
services [drop]. Changing them without stepping down is something he finds
"WAY too hard for me to know how we can plan for at this stage of our
bootstrap". It gets a door. Turn the page.

